pool.setUserUseReserveAsCollateral()
├── given not active
   └── it should revert
├── given paused
   └── it should revert
├── given frozen
   └── it should succeed
├── when the flag already matches the requested state
    ├── when enabling and the flag is already enabled
        └── it succeeds with a no-op [01]
    └── when disabling and the flag is already disabled
        └── it succeeds with a no-op, even with a zero aToken balance [02]
├── when enabling
   ├── when the user's scaled aToken balance is zero
      └── it should revert
   ├── when the asset has a zero LTV
      └── it should revert
   ├── when the user is in isolation mode
      └── it should revert
   ├── when the asset is isolated and the user is already using another asset as collateral
      └── it should revert
   └── when the user has a balance and validation passes
      └── it should succeed, enabling the flag and emitting ReserveUsedAsCollateralEnabled [03]
└── when disabling
   ├── when the resulting health factor is below 1
      └── it should revert (boundary)
   ├── when the user holds other zero-LTV collateral and the disabled asset has a nonzero LTV
      └── it should revert
   └── when the resulting position stays healthy
      └── it should succeed, disabling the flag and emitting ReserveUsedAsCollateralDisabled [04]
